TEST 3116 -- BGPv4 - Unicast Traffic
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22, tb470

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- BENCH LIMIT, not a product or scope issue.

The case's assertion is a RATE one: "Run background unicast traffic ... Line
rate traffic is achieved as expected."

This harness injects with scapy at ~26 Mbps -- 2.6% of a gigabit port -- so
"line rate is achieved" cannot be demonstrated or refuted. Counting packets at
low offered load would show 10/10 and prove nothing about line rate.

WHAT IS PROVEN ELSEWHERE: the BGP4+ session itself is established and stable
across disconnect/reconnect (T3114, 3/3) and carries a default route end to end
with the peer installing it (T3111). So the control plane this case rides on is
demonstrated; only the throughput claim is out of reach.

TO UNBLOCK: a line-rate traffic generator -- the same requirement as QoS
13549/13553, switching 12067, and the guest-VLAN rate cases.
